added_lemmas.statement:
Let \(\ell=\log(en)\), fix \(\kappa\in K\) and \(P\in\mathrm{Base}_\kappa\), and put \(\mathcal F_1=\sigma(O_i:i\in I_1)\).  Condition on the first-half scores.  Let \(\eta:B\to H_n\) be any Borel selector which is constant on each cell, including singleton breakpoint cells, of a finite first-half breakpoint arrangement.
For \(i\in I_2\), define
\[
 \varepsilon_i=Y_i-T_i m_{1,P}(X_i)-(1-T_i)m_{0,P}(X_i).
\]
Then there are constants \(C_0,C\), uniform for \(\kappa\in K\), such that
\[
\begin{aligned}
 &E_P\!\left[
 \sup_{\substack{x\in B,\ t\in\{0,1\}\\N_t^{(2)}(x,\eta(x))>0}}
 \left|
 \frac{\sum_{i\in I_2}\varepsilon_i
 \mathbf 1\{X_i\in A_t,\ \|X_i-x\|_2\leq\eta(x)\}}
 {N_t^{(2)}(x,\eta(x))}
 \right|\,\middle|\,\mathcal F_1\right]\\
 &\qquad\leq
 C\sup_{x\in B}\sigma\sqrt{
 \frac{1+\log\!\left(
 e\left\{1\vee J_P\!\left(
 \eta(x),\min\{1,C_0a_P(x,\eta(x))\}\right)\right\}\right)}
 {n_2a_P(x,\eta(x))}}
 +C\sigma\frac{\ell^2}{n}.                                      \tag{M2}
\end{aligned}
\]
In particular, taking \(\eta=\widehat h\) proves the stochastic assertion in equation \((23)\) of the oracle proof without a factor \(|H_n|\), \(\log |H_n|\), or the number of severity layers.
